## Who is responsible for your data

Data controller: [EMPRESA], NIF [NIF], address: [DIRECCIÓN]. Send questions about your data to [EMAIL].

## What data we collect

- from the request form: name, phone, preferred way of contact, field of work and city, whether you are already in Spain, comment;
- from the site chat: your messages, your name and, if you wish, your phone;
- if you write to us on Telegram, WhatsApp or Viber: your name or username, phone number and the conversation;
- from employers: company name, contact person, phone, job description;
- technical data: IP address (spam protection), site language, where you came from (ad link, UTM tags);
- anonymous visit statistics: a random browser identifier, pages viewed, time on the site. They contain no name, phone or IP address.

## Why and on what legal basis

- to contact you and find a job or service for you — your consent given in the form (art. 6.1.a GDPR);
- to pass your application to an employer — only with your consent, which the manager will ask for separately;
- to protect the site from spam and abuse — our legitimate interest (art. 6.1.f GDPR);
- anonymous statistics to improve the site — our legitimate interest;
- to comply with the law — legal obligation (art. 6.1.c GDPR).

## Do you have to give us data

A request needs your name and phone so a manager can contact you; without them it cannot be handled. In the site chat the phone is optional — the reply comes to the chat window. Other fields are optional.

## Who we share data with

- employers — only with your consent and only what is needed for the selection;
- providers processing data on our behalf: hosting [PROVEEDOR DE HOSTING] (servers in the EU);
- Telegram, WhatsApp (Meta) and Viber — if you choose to talk to us there. These companies may process data outside the EU under their own policies and the EU standard contractual clauses;
- public authorities — only when required by law.

We do not sell your data.

## How long we keep data

- requests and conversations — up to 24 months after your last contact, then the data is anonymised;
- visit statistics — up to 13 months;
- data in your browser (saved jobs, saved name and phone) — until you delete it.

## Your rights

You can at any time access your data, correct it, delete it, restrict or object to its processing, receive it in a portable format and withdraw your consent (this does not affect processing before the withdrawal). Write to [EMAIL] — we reply within one month.

If you believe your rights have been violated, you can complain to the Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD): www.aepd.es.

## Minors

The site is intended for people aged 16 and over. We do not knowingly collect data of younger people.

## Automated decisions

We do not make automated decisions about you or build profiles.

## Cookies and browser data

See the "Cookie policy" page.

## Changes

Version of [FECHA]. Each request is stored together with the policy version you agreed to.

